! Proposed Definitions and Examples

!! cmavo: .a (A)

!!! Proposed Definition
A sumti ALC such that the containing bridi is true if and only if it is true for at least one of the connected sumti.

!!! Proposed Keywords
* or (sumti)
* inclusive or (sumti)
* and/or (sumti)

!!! Usage Examples
;.i ju'o la .alis. .a la .bab. djuno:I’m sure Alice or Bob knows.
;.i mi na ponse lo jdini .a lo kacma;I have neither money nor a camera.

!! cmavo: .e (A)

!!! Proposed Definition
A sumti ALC such that the containing bridi is true if and only if it is true for each of the connected sumti.

!!! Proposed Keywords
* and (sumti)
* but (sumti)

!!! Usage Examples
;.i makfa do .e nai mi:Magic to you but not to me.

----

!! Proposed Definition of ''ji''

;__ji__ (A): sumti conn ? -- logical connective: sumti afterthought connective question --
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''ji'' Usage

;.i do djica tu'a lo jipci ji tu'a lo finpe:Do you want chicken or fish or both or neither or ...?

A possible answer could be "na.e", meaning "Not the chicken, the fish." But it can actually get even weirder, because ".a nai", for example, is perfictly valid, and would mean something like "I want fish only if I also want chicken". And you can always answer with a simple ".a" if you want to be obstinate and give no useful information.

!! Proposed Definition of ''na.a''

;__na.a__ (A*): sumti only if -- logical connective: sumti afterthought conditional/only if --
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''na.a'' Usage

;.i mi djica tu'a lo jipci na.a tu'a lo finpe:I want chicken only if I want fish.

!! Proposed Definition of ''.o''

;__.o__ (A): sumti iff -- logical connective: sumti afterthought biconditional/iff/if-and-only-if --
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''.o'' Usage

;.i mi djica tu'a lo jipci .o tu'a lo finpe:I want chicken if and only if I want chicken. (This might be implied in English anyway using "if" instead of "if and only if")

!! Proposed Definition of ''.onai''

;__.onai__ (A*): sumti xor -- logical connective: sumti afterthought exclusive or; Latin 'aut' --
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''.onai'' Usage

;.i mi djica tu'a lo jipci .onai tu'a lo finpe:I want either chicken or fish (not both).

!! Proposed Definition of ''.u''

;__.u__ (A): sumti whether -- logical connective: sumti afterthought whether-or-not --
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''.u'' Usage

;.i mi djica tu'a lo jipci .u tu'a lo finpe:I want chicken whether or not I want the fish.

